<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sima Cuo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 4th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sima Cuo was a general of the state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qin-dynasty">Qin</a> under King Huiwen. In 316 BCE he argued successfully for conquering Shu rather than attacking the Zhou royal domain, and he then conquered Shu and Ba, giving Qin the rich <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sichuan">Sichuan</a> basin. He later campaigned against Chu and was an ancestor of the historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sima-qian">Sima Qian</a>.</p></div>
